alrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/monday-assorted-links-567.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-567">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/emollick/status/2072872373758382497</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/emollick/status/2072872373758382497</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 15:49:36 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[A lot of them should have been fired anyway]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HMQ-PZAbAAA5B3Z.jpg:large"></p><p>KingoftheCoast (@kingofthecoastt) on X</p><p>Pretty compelling evidence (from Denmark) in favor of Truman Bewley’s thesis that firms do not view nominal wage cuts as substitutes for layoffs. Both because of morale effects &amp; because layoffs are used adjust the workforce composition. An overall win for sticky wages.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/kingofthecoastt/status/2072851416809619663">https://x.com/kingofthecoastt/status/2072851416809619663</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/monday-assorted-links-567.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-567">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/kingofthecoastt/status/2072851416809619663</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/kingofthecoastt/status/2072851416809619663</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 15:49:36 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[The world’s first fully robot-run hotel in China?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://tech.yahoo.com/general/articles/world-first-fully-robot-run-184455211.html?utm_source=getsuperintel.site&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=meta-s-watermelon-llm-catches-gpt-5-5&_bhlid=7157d1d4df4a2f0e701ff920a9a2494938d1aab9">https://tech.yahoo.com/general/articles/world-first-fully-robot-run-184455211.html?utm_source=getsuperintel.site&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=meta-s-watermelon-llm-catches-gpt-5